course: dictionary
lesson: 3966
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists several, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Look at the clues around the word: the topic, the other words, and what is happening. «The Sun shines because tiny parts of hydrogen join together deep inside it, a process called fusion.» The topic is stars and the clue is join together, so fusion means joining things into one.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another place. «Fusion food mixes cooking from different countries.» Here fusion has nothing to do with stars. It means a mix of styles. Ask yourself which meaning fits this topic, then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Phrases are helpful clues too. In «nuclear fusion», the word nuclear points to science. In «a fusion of», the words that follow tell you two or more things have been mixed or joined together.
fact: Fusion means the joining of two or more things into one.
fact: Nuclear fusion is when tiny atoms join together and give out huge amounts of energy.
fact: Nuclear fusion is how the Sun shines, so it gives us light and heat.
fact: Fusion food mixes cooking from different countries.
fact: Fusion can also mean melting, especially of metal or rock.
exercise: «The Sun shines because tiny parts of hydrogen join together deep inside it, a process called fusion.» What is fusion here? | A cloud of gas and dust | Melting ice on a frozen lake | *Tiny atoms joining together to give out energy | Cooking food from two countries
exercise: Ada's dinner mixes Indian and British cooking. What is a word for this kind of food? | *Fusion food | Nebula | Protostar | Melting
exercise: «Jupiter is far too small to start fusion.» Why can Jupiter not start fusion? | It has no gravity | *It is too small | It is too old to glow | It is too far from the Sun
test: In «a fusion of jazz and rock», what does fusion mean? | *A mix of two styles | Very old music | A clump of dust | Tiny atoms joining in the Sun
test: What is nuclear fusion? | *Tiny atoms joining together and giving out huge energy | Rock being cut into small pieces | Music from two countries | Gas and dust collapsing into a cloud
exam: Fusion can also mean the melting of metal or rock. Which word is closest in meaning? | *Melting | Cooking | Gravity | Nebula
